{"event":"intent","sources":["f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=xmit-softirq-lock; Search only snapshots/s01 and no other snapshot. Hunt the exact seed shape: a driver spinlock taken with plain spin_lock() (missing spin_lock_bh or local_bh_disable) in process-context or workqueue-context code (xmit workers, hw-tx/enqueue helpers, firmware, ioctl, open, SME/request handlers) where the same lock object is also acquired on a path reachable from ndo_start_xmit or TX-completion callbacks that run under NET_TX/NET_RX softirq, so a softirq on the same CPU spins forever against a holder that can never resume (soft-lockup, RCU stall, TX-stall denial of service). For every candidate record the lock name, the softirq-side and process-side call chains with file:line, and the missing bottom-half-disable guarantee; the staging ks7010 tx_dev_lock seed is a demonstration only and must never be reported. Save a structured artifact for snapshots/s01 with candidates plus exact source evidence, or a negative result backed by concrete source evidence."}
